&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tailscale&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tailscale is making safe connection effortless by delivering software that makes it easy to securely interconnect people and their devices, no matter where they are. From hobbyists to multinational corporations, teams of every size use Tailscale each day to protect their networks, share access to internal tools, and more. We&#39;re building a future for the Internet that&#39;s easy, sensible, and safe, like it used to be. Founded in 2019 and fully distributed, we&#39;re backed by Accel, CRV, Insight, Heavybit, and Uncork Capital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we grow, integrations are becoming an increasingly important part of how customers build with Tailscale. We&#39;re looking for an Integration Partnerships Lead to help identify, develop, and launch the technical partnerships that extend our products and make Tailscale more valuable alongside the tools our customers already use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on &lt;strong&gt;technical partnerships role at the intersection of Sales Engineering and Partner Development&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll work directly with technology partners, customers, Product, and Engineering to identify integration opportunities, understand technical requirements, design solutions, establish the partnership, and help take integrations from concept through launch and adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll initially focus on integrations across Aperture, Privileged Access Management (PAM), and VPN, working with partners across AI, security, identity, infrastructure, developer tools, and adjacent technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who can move comfortably between a technical architecture conversation and a commercial partnership discussion. You should be able to understand how two products work together, explain the customer value, navigate APIs and integration requirements, build relationships with technical and business stakeholders, and drive both organizations toward a successful launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop high-value technology and integration partnerships based on customer needs, product priorities, and market opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own partner opportunities from initial outreach and technical discovery through solution design, commercial alignment, launch, and ongoing adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical discovery with partners and customers to understand architectures, APIs, authentication, security requirements, data flows, and integration use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product and Engineering to assess technical feasibility, define integration requirements, and determine the right implementation approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships across partner Product, Engineering, Sales, and Business Development teams while serving as the primary point of contact at Tailscale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the technical and business case for integrations, including customer value, use cases, implementation requirements, and commercial opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal and Finance on agreements, pricing, packaging, licensing, and revenue-sharing structures where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Sales, Solutions Engineering, Marketing, and Customer Success to launch integrations and drive customer and partner adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring customer, partner, and market feedback back to Product and Engineering to help inform future integration priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish repeatable approaches for evaluating, building, launching, and scaling technology partnerships as the ecosystem grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
