&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Product Manager to own Tailscale&#39;s Identity ecosystem — the bridge between our &quot;Zero Trust&quot; networking philosophy and the existing identity infrastructure our customers already rely on. Identity is the foundation of access control in Tailscale; if a user cannot authenticate or authorize correctly, the network cannot be secure. In this role, you will bridge the gap between complex security protocols (OIDC, SAML, SCIM) and a seamless, &quot;it just works&quot; user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Identity portfolio covers the end-to-end lifecycle of a user and device within the tailnet:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Authentication:&lt;/strong&gt; Integrating with external Identity Providers (IdPs) so users can log in using the credentials they already have (Okta, Azure AD, Google Workspace, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Authorization:&lt;/strong&gt; Defining how roles, groups, and attributes translate into granular network access policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lifecycle Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Automating the onboarding, offboarding, and synchronization (SCIM) of users and devices as they change roles or leave organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These capabilities are where Tailscale meets the customer&#39;s existing security stack. Nearly every enterprise deployment begins with an identity integration, grows through complex multi-IdP setups, and increasingly depends on automated lifecycle management for production security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision, strategy, and roadmap for Tailscale&#39;s Identity portfolio: workload and agent identity, SSO integrations, Directory Sync (SCIM), access controls and policy, user management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operator experience for admins: How IT and security teams configure identity providers, audit authentication events, and manage user, workload, and agent access policies at scale, across the admin console, API, and clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a best-in-class authentication experience for end-users: Save our users time and money by making every auth flow fast, secure, and intuitive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely across engineering, product, and design org to ensure Tailscale’s identity service meets the needs of the broader organization and integrates tightly with other platform components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build systematic customer insight across the full spread of Tailscale users, from a homelab operator exposing a media server through Funnel to a regulated enterprise routing traffic across multi-region datacenters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn customer signal, support patterns, cross-product requests, and competitive dynamics into roadmap priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–7 years in product management, with direct ownership of an identity product or platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency in identity protocols: Comfortable engaging engineers as a peer on OIDC, SAML, SCIM, WebAuthn, and OAuth flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping products for developer or security-focused audiences: You understand the friction points of modern IAM and know how to build tools that admins and developers actually enjoy using.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own a product area end to end: Strategy, roadmap, execution, and the customer relationships that keep you honest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational mindset: You understand that for an identity product, downtime or misconfiguration isn&#39;t just a bug—it’s a security event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Tailscale at work or home.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working with specific Identity Providers (Okta, Azure Entra ID/Active Directory, Google Workspace) or Identity-Aware Proxy (IAP) architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
