&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for considering Tailscale. If this job description resonates with you, please apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Frequently cited statistics show that people who identify with historically marginalized groups are likely to apply to jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We encourage you to help us break that statistic!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tailscale&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tailscale is making safe connection effortless by delivering software that makes it easy to securely interconnect people and their devices, no matter where they are. From hobbyists to multinational corporations, teams of every size use Tailscale each day to protect their networks, share access to internal tools, and more. We&#39;re building a future for the Internet that&#39;s easy, sensible, and safe, like it used to be. Founded in 2019 and fully distributed, we&#39;re backed by Accel, CRV, Insight, Heavybit, and Uncork Capital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Product Manager to own Tailscale&#39;s networking features — the layer that decides how traffic finds its destination by &lt;em&gt;name&lt;/em&gt; on top of Tailscale’s seamless mesh connectivity solution. Concretely, you will own four feature sets: &lt;strong&gt;App Connectors&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;DNS&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Funnel&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Tailscale Serve &amp;amp; Services&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A tailnet gives every device an identity and an address. Networking features are what turn addresses into something a person, a script, or an AI agent can actually use — a name, a service, an app, a URL.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;App Connectors&lt;/strong&gt; route traffic to specific SaaS and private applications by name, so access follows the app rather than the IP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DNS&lt;/strong&gt; — MagicDNS, split DNS, custom name servers, search domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tailscale Serve &amp;amp; Services&lt;/strong&gt; make a workload — not a machine — the unit of connectivity and access: addressable, load-balanced, and durable across the instances behind it. This is the wedge that lets customers replace a service registry, and eventually much of what they use a service mesh for, with Tailscale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Funnel&lt;/strong&gt; is Tailscale&#39;s ingress story: securely exposing a Service running inside the tailnet to the public internet, from a hobbyist sharing a dev server to production webhooks and public endpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the most user-visible role in Tailscale&#39;s Dataplane Platform, and the work is as much product design as it is networking. DNS settings, connector topologies, and service definitions are configured by network engineers and IT admins in the admin console, API, and CLI, and the distance between &quot;magical&quot; and &quot;unusable&quot; is the object model, the defaults, and the error messages.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href=&quot;https://tailscale.com/blog/how-tailscale-works&quot;&gt;How Tailscale Works&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://tailscale.com/kb/1223/funnel&quot;&gt;Tailscale Funnel&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://tailscale.com/blog/four-ways-tailscale-service&quot;&gt;Four ways to Tailscale a service&lt;/a&gt; to learn more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision, strategy, and roadmap for Tailscale&#39;s networking features: App Connectors, DNS, Funnel, and Tailscale Services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operator experience across these surfaces: how network engineers and IT admins configure, segment, monitor, and troubleshoot them at scale, in both the admin console and the CLI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM, Customer Success, and Solutions Engineering on production commitments and strategic deals, and champion the migration path from reverse proxies, bastion hosts, cloud ingress, and service meshes to Tailscale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build systematic customer insight across the full spread of Tailscale users, from a homelab operator exposing a media server through Funnel to a large enterprise replacing its service registry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in product management, including direct ownership of an application-layer connectivity product: reverse proxies, ingress controllers or gateways, API gateways, service mesh or service registry, DNS and traffic management, secure tunneling and exposure products, or identity-aware proxy connectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of turning a complex networking system into a legible product surface: you can point to an object model, a set of defaults, or a configuration experience you designed and explain why it was right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end ownership of a product area: strategy, requirements, launch (docs, enablement, rollout), and the iteration after launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of data-informed decisions — metrics you defined, instrumentation you pushed for, and at least one time the data changed your mind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Nice To Have&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Product Led Growth and how to balance that with enterprise buying motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes networking: ingress, Gateway API, operators, or service exposure patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with secure tunneling and exposure products (ngrok, Cloudflare Tunnel, Cloudflare Access, Teleport, Zscaler Private Access) as a builder or a heavy user&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Abuse prevention, rate limiting, or trust and safety work on a publicly exposed service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with VPN and tunneling protocols (WireGuard, IPsec), BGP, cloud VPC peering, or PrivateLink-style private connectivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public technical writing, conference talks, or open-source contributions in networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Tailscale at work or at home&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
