&lt;li&gt;5+ years in engineering operations, release management, or a closely related role at a software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience building or significantly improving release management processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency: you understand software development deeply enough to have credible conversations with engineers about build systems, deployment pipelines, branching strategies, and production operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong instincts for what process is worth having and what’s just overhead, and optimizing process for trust and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and the ability to build structure from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
