&lt;p&gt;You will work as part of the Program Management team to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roadmap health&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy and standards for roadmap health, including how initiative and epic dates and health are defined, tracked, and reported.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve the Product org’s continuous planning cadence as the company grows, and connect it to company planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the external roadmap and how it’s communicated to customers and the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product launch health&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the launch framework and readiness standards used across Product, PMM, Sales, and Support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with PMM, Sales, and Support leaders to make launch readiness consistent and measurable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Internal documentation and onboarding&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the standards for how Product org documentation is structured and maintained, so teams can keep it current themselves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the Product team’s onboarding program as the org grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Feature request health&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the end-to-end feature request system, from intake in Jira to its connection with roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give Product leadership a clear view of demand and how it’s reflected in the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customer insight&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a single customer insight strategy that combines closed-lost data, feature requests, QBRs, and community feedback from Discord, Reddit, and GitHub into a view that informs prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating rhythms&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Product org’s operating model, including the customer QBR process for EPD and the internal MBR, and evolve them as needs change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data health&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the Product org’s metrics and data strategy, partnering with Data so dashboards scale with new products and features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Across all areas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently identify gaps in how Product operates, make the case to leadership, and drive solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product leadership on priorities and trade-offs, bringing recommendations rather than status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Role Success&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is successful when Product leadership relies on product operations as a strategic partner, customer insight visibly shapes the roadmap, and the Product org’s operating model scales as Tailscale adds products and teams.&lt;/p&gt;
